      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0136",
      "sequence": 148,
      "meaning": "Looking again in the water, Nārada recovers his own form, but his heart remains unsatisfied. His lips trembling with rage, he rushes to Lakṣmī’s Lord, intending either to curse him or die, and meets the enemy of demons on the road with Lakṣmī in the form of the same princess. Sweetly Hari asks where the distraught sage is going. Deluded beyond reason, Nārada erupts: Hari cannot bear another’s prosperity and is uniquely jealous and deceitful; at the ocean-churning he maddened Śiva into drinking poison, gave liquor to the demons, poison to Śiva, and kept Lakṣmī and the lovely jewel for himself. He accuses the independent Lord of crookedly pursuing self-interest.",
