    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0137",
      "sequence": 149,
      "meaning": "Nārada continues: with no master above him, Hari does whatever pleases him, turning good into bad and bad into good without wonder, joy or regret; he deceives everyone fearlessly because karma cannot bind him and no one has yet subdued him. But now, Nārada says, Hari has met the right opponent and will reap his deed. He curses the Lord to assume the very human body used to deceive him; monkeys will assist him because he gave Nārada a monkey’s form, and separation from a woman will bring him deep sorrow. Hari joyfully accepts the curse and humbly petitions the sage, then compassionately draws away the overpowering māyā.",
