    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0138",
      "sequence": 150,
      "meaning": "When Hari removes his māyā, neither Lakṣmī nor the princess is there. Terrified, Nārada clings to Hari’s feet and begs the compassionate saviour of the surrendered to make his curse false and tell him how the sin of his many harsh words can be erased. Hari directs him to repeat Śaṅkara’s hundred names, assuring immediate peace, and tells him never to abandon the conviction that no one is as dear to Hari as Śiva; without Purāri’s grace, no one gains Hari’s devotion. Holding this in his heart, Nārada is to wander the earth beyond māyā’s reach. After instructing him in many ways, the Lord disappears, and Nārada travels to Brahmā’s realm singing Rāma’s virtues.",
