    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0139",
      "sequence": 151,
      "meaning": "On the road Śiva’s attendants see the now-undeluded, joyful Nārada and approach him in fear. Clasping his feet, they confess they are not Brahmins and have suffered for their grave offence, and beg him to turn the curse into a blessing. Nārada says they will indeed become two powerful, glorious night-rangers and conquer the world; when Viṣṇu assumes a human body, they will die by his hand in battle, be liberated, and not return to worldly existence. The pair bow and depart, becoming demons in due course. For this reason the Lord assumed a human incarnation in one cosmic cycle, delighting gods and good people and relieving the earth’s burden.",
