    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0140",
      "sequence": 152,
      "meaning": "Hari’s births and deeds are thus beautiful, joyful, wondrous and innumerable. In every cosmic cycle the Lord descends and performs lovely deeds of many kinds; sages sing them in supremely purifying narratives and the wise should not be surprised by differing episodes. Hari is infinite and so are Hari’s stories: even through millions of cycles Rāmacandra’s lovely deeds cannot be exhausted. Śiva says he told this episode to show how Hari’s māyā deludes even a wise sage. The playful Lord is easy for devotees to reach and removes every sorrow, yet no god, human or sage is beyond mighty māyā; therefore one should worship māyā’s Lord.",
